                <pb facs="0791" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 840.48/153</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé d’Affaires in Russia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-10T04:00:00+02:30">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 10, 1914, 4 a.m.</hi>
                    </date> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Department’s telegram 6th instant. Russian Government does not fully understand
                    inquiry but says it would not interfere with neutral vessels which may be
                    chartered by citizens’ committee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
